WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:07.005
Hi, I'm Derrick Dennis. I specialize in

00:00:07.005 --> 00:00:09.660
repairing and cleaning washing machines,

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:11.703
dryers, any major appliances.

00:00:13.710 --> 00:00:15.990
The two main types of washing
machines that I work on

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:17.580
are top-loaders and front-loaders.

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:19.380
I'm going to show you how I clean them.

00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:23.100
So, this top-load washer is, I would say,

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:25.350
between 15 and 17 years old.

00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:27.342
This machine here hasn't been cleaned,

00:00:27.342 --> 00:00:29.700
I would say, ever since it was purchased.

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:31.410
The biggest problem with this,

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:34.080
the abundance of buildup
from excessive use

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:36.120
of detergent, fabric softener,

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:37.080
all the buildup you see,

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:39.240
that's what causes this
big ring around the top.

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:40.530
The water doesn't come up that high.

00:00:40.530 --> 00:00:42.420
That's why you see the different levels.

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:44.220
And then the buildup of mold.

00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:47.123
The perfect, ideal circumstance for mold

00:00:47.123 --> 00:00:51.240
and mildew buildup is
moisture, darkness, and heat.

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:53.340
So common buildup in these machines

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:56.130
due to overuse of
high-efficiency detergent

00:00:56.130 --> 00:00:58.110
and fabric softener, which you don't need.

00:00:58.110 --> 00:01:00.330
This big buildup, you're
going to get rust,

00:01:00.330 --> 00:01:02.820
you're going to get mold, mildew.

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:05.400
2 tablespoons of high-efficiency detergent

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:06.690
and no fabric softener

00:01:06.690 --> 00:01:09.540
will make your machine last ages longer

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:13.080
than if you're dumping a cup
or two of fabric softener.

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:15.300
And it doesn't get your
clothes any cleaner.

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:17.400
I highly recommend cutting
out fabric softener

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:19.050
in your laundry regimen.

00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:21.540
The reason that I'm so
against fabric softener

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:23.310
is when you use fabric softener,

00:01:23.310 --> 00:01:26.370
the reason that it works is
the reason that it's bad.

00:01:26.370 --> 00:01:28.710
So it builds up like an oily residue,

00:01:28.710 --> 00:01:31.200
because those enzymes have
been trapped inside your shirt,

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:33.060
and so that's what causes it to smell.

00:01:33.060 --> 00:01:35.767
So it's not because of
you, but eventually,

00:01:35.767 --> 00:01:37.740
the overuse of high-efficiency detergent

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:40.156
and fabric softener will
cause your clothes to smell,

00:01:40.156 --> 00:01:42.060
even if they're clean.

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:43.530
So, anytime we maintenance a machine,

00:01:43.530 --> 00:01:44.940
we want to make sure
that we're unplugging it

00:01:44.940 --> 00:01:46.200
from any power source,

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:48.030
and it's good to cut the water off.

00:01:48.030 --> 00:01:50.730
So, generally we start
from top to the bottom.

00:01:50.730 --> 00:01:53.130
The main thing is removing the tub

00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:55.350
and cleaning the inner and outer baskets.

00:01:55.350 --> 00:01:57.483
That's where all of your smell comes from.

00:01:59.310 --> 00:02:00.630
With these direct-drive machines,

00:02:00.630 --> 00:02:03.060
a lot of times we have,
the legs are rusty,

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:05.760
and we'll either scrape
them down, repaint them,

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:07.470
make sure we knock the cobwebs out,

00:02:07.470 --> 00:02:08.303
all that kind of stuff.

00:02:08.303 --> 00:02:09.900
Sometimes we'll find a little baby sock.

00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:11.460
You never know.

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:13.080
We like to use toothbrushes,

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:15.030
different-style brushes.

00:02:15.030 --> 00:02:16.650
You have pointy brushes, flat brushes.

00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:18.150
They all have different jobs,

00:02:18.150 --> 00:02:20.670
but brushes are very key.

00:02:20.670 --> 00:02:22.560
They're vital to everything we do.

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:24.630
So the brushes really help to get in there

00:02:24.630 --> 00:02:26.850
and kind of get in the
corners and the crevices

00:02:26.850 --> 00:02:28.863
to clean all this mildew and mold out.

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:32.130
Sometimes the pressure washer

00:02:32.130 --> 00:02:33.750
doesn't get inside the balance ring,

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:35.580
and we have some bristles in there

00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:38.190
and kind of really put
some elbow grease in it.

00:02:38.190 --> 00:02:41.850
My favorite cleaner is
Pine-Sol, bleach, Lysol.

00:02:41.850 --> 00:02:44.460
Vinegar is more of what I recommend

00:02:44.460 --> 00:02:47.490
for people to use through a washing cycle.

00:02:47.490 --> 00:02:50.340
White distilled vinegar
has acetic compounds

00:02:50.340 --> 00:02:52.623
that help kill some bacterias.

00:02:54.330 --> 00:02:57.030
When we pressure wash,
first we start the outside.

00:02:57.030 --> 00:02:59.490
We can get a lot better
into the balance ring.

00:02:59.490 --> 00:03:00.450
A pressure washer,

00:03:00.450 --> 00:03:03.330
the water finds its ways
into all the crevices,

00:03:03.330 --> 00:03:05.370
and it does a much better job

00:03:05.370 --> 00:03:07.740
at pushing out all this mold and mildew

00:03:07.740 --> 00:03:10.350
and detergent buildup and
fabric-softener buildup

00:03:10.350 --> 00:03:11.183
all the way out of the holes.

00:03:11.183 --> 00:03:12.690
Then we can just rinse
it out of the inside,

00:03:12.690 --> 00:03:15.660
and we have pretty much
a brand-new basket.

00:03:15.660 --> 00:03:17.550
So, the steam cleaning usually comes

00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:18.810
after the pressure washing

00:03:18.810 --> 00:03:21.720
just because we want to
get kind of a final clean.

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:23.340
The best thing about the steamer

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:26.220
is the water comes out at
a superhigh temperature,

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:28.410
and that helps to effectively sanitize

00:03:28.410 --> 00:03:30.180
any of these crevices or cracks

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:31.440
or anything that we can't just clean

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:33.213
with a pressure washer or bleach.

00:03:35.970 --> 00:03:38.010
So, the front-loader,
the cleaning process,

00:03:38.010 --> 00:03:41.460
it's similar, but it's a lot
different in the disassembly

00:03:41.460 --> 00:03:44.010
and just the orientation of the basket.

00:03:44.010 --> 00:03:46.950
I can't remove a basket all
the way from a front-loader.

00:03:46.950 --> 00:03:49.260
I can only clean the front half.

00:03:49.260 --> 00:03:51.120
The old-school top-loaders
are built like tanks.

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:52.380
The front-loaders are not,

00:03:52.380 --> 00:03:54.390
but they clean your clothes better.

00:03:54.390 --> 00:03:56.942
They generally don't need as much cleaning

00:03:56.942 --> 00:03:59.100
as a top-loader because of the orientation

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:01.737
and the way the water spins inside,

00:04:01.737 --> 00:04:04.590
and the water actually
keeps the tubs cleaner.

00:04:04.590 --> 00:04:06.180
The biggest part of the smell that we see

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:09.180
is from pump building up
lint and debris in there

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:10.620
and people not cleaning it out.

00:04:10.620 --> 00:04:12.480
And then you stay with a smell,

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:15.870
or because people don't
wipe out their door seal

00:04:15.870 --> 00:04:17.130
every time they use the machine,

00:04:17.130 --> 00:04:18.600
they keep the door closed,

00:04:18.600 --> 00:04:21.330
and then that just
builds up a mildew smell.

00:04:21.330 --> 00:04:22.680
As long as you keep the door open

00:04:22.680 --> 00:04:24.480
and wipe the door seal out

00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:27.180
and run a washer-cleaner tablet through

00:04:27.180 --> 00:04:29.254
once a month or so,
white distilled vinegar,

00:04:29.254 --> 00:04:31.740
it's not going to smell.
I can guarantee it.

00:04:31.740 --> 00:04:33.150
So, with this front loader,

00:04:33.150 --> 00:04:35.760
it actually has a clean-out
spot for the lint.

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:37.050
This is what protects your pump,

00:04:37.050 --> 00:04:40.350
and this is what helps keep
the smell down internally.

00:04:40.350 --> 00:04:41.340
Pull the door down.

00:04:41.340 --> 00:04:43.110
We drain the water out of this little,

00:04:43.110 --> 00:04:44.872
this is the drain hose that actually pulls

00:04:44.872 --> 00:04:47.010
whatever water is left inside the pump.

00:04:47.010 --> 00:04:48.990
And then we take the
filter out, clean it out,

00:04:48.990 --> 00:04:50.665
and that's it. It's that simple.

00:04:50.665 --> 00:04:52.620
I recommend doing this every 30 days,

00:04:52.620 --> 00:04:54.030
at least every six months,

00:04:54.030 --> 00:04:55.268
and this is going to prevent odor.

00:04:55.268 --> 00:04:57.030
It's going to keep your washing machine

00:04:57.030 --> 00:04:59.070
lasting a whole lot longer.

00:04:59.070 --> 00:05:02.340
The average life span of
pretty much any washer

00:05:02.340 --> 00:05:04.650
is two or three years
before the bearings go out,

00:05:04.650 --> 00:05:06.150
you know, just because of,

00:05:06.150 --> 00:05:09.330
and that really comes from
the overuse of detergent.

00:05:09.330 --> 00:05:11.670
So when a detergent breaks
down that oil and grease,

00:05:11.670 --> 00:05:14.310
it'll cause the bearings
to get rusted, rusty,

00:05:14.310 --> 00:05:15.840
and then your washing machine will sound

00:05:15.840 --> 00:05:17.340
like a jet plane taking off.

00:05:17.340 --> 00:05:18.210
That's bad bearings.

00:05:18.210 --> 00:05:19.140
It's really hard to get to

00:05:19.140 --> 00:05:21.300
if you can't physically
tear these things down

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:22.530
and clean them yourself.

00:05:22.530 --> 00:05:24.930
So the best thing to do
is preventive maintenance.

00:05:24.930 --> 00:05:26.730
2 tablespoons of detergent,

00:05:26.730 --> 00:05:29.007
no fabric softener at all,
but if you have to use it,

00:05:29.007 --> 00:05:30.840
make sure you dilute it by 50%.

00:05:30.840 --> 00:05:32.760
You know, when I sell
a machine to somebody,

00:05:32.760 --> 00:05:33.750
I want them to have faith

00:05:33.750 --> 00:05:35.820
that I have sold them the
cleanest used washing machine

00:05:35.820 --> 00:05:37.203
that they can possibly buy.

